  "notes": [
    "The material is 123 islands and no flow joins two. Each island is a short list of components with findings, and the chains it gives are declared with it, so the counts below are by construction. The test re-derives them from the committed files with its own coding of S-3, which is the check that the declaration and the files agree.",
    "120 consolidated chains: more than the 105 at which S-3(g)'s bound bites. At most five surface, so 115 are not shown in full, 100 of them get a compact row and the last line states how many are not listed (15).",
    "Surfacing (S-3(f)): the V island's two chains end at one finding. Whichever ranks first surfaces, and carries converging 1; the other ranks within the first few places and is passed over. It is not surfaced, so it has a compact row.",
    "candidates minus consolidated is the sum of the three drops: tails that fold into a longer chain, a mutual pair's second chain, and chains with no Critical or High finding. chains.json does not carry the drops, so only their sum is checkable against a script.",
    "Closure: closure-2 and closure-3 have no flow between the two components that carry findings. The link exists only through the transitive closure.",
    "Direction: in closure-3, in some other special islands and in one plain island in three, the flow runs against the link, so the link's source component cannot reach its target and only the other way round holds. Such a chain has against_flow true. It exists only if reachability counts in either direction (orchestrator.md Phase 3.5 step 2, 'or vice versa'; ADR-050 D13, 'one component is reachable from the other'), which is how the rule stands (S-3(b), unchanged). Narrowing it to the link's direction is an R-21 change, and the chains that need it are counts.against_flow of the consolidated ones.",
    "Left out of chain formation: AG and LLM findings, and STRIDE findings on an unclassified layer. Six such findings sit on components that a flow joins to a chain's components, so a script that forgot the rule would see them.",
    "A chain's breaking target follows the orchestrator's Step 4. The V island's two arms use both tie-breaks of the 4-finding rule: the higher severity, then the earlier position.",
    "The compact rows are in the shipped format of contracts/threat-model-records.md. A row's layers and findings are in chain order.",
    "Not reached here: a finding with more than one onward link (S-3(c)'s choice among candidates, which no island needs), and a chain that is a run in the middle of another. The tests of attack-chains.py build those inline.",
    "How to run: copy run/ to a working directory and rename its tachi-build/ to .tachi-build/ (.gitignore excludes that name, so the committed copy cannot hold it). Then run attack-chains.py with --run-dir on the working directory."
